| ID | Requirement |
|---|---|
| UX-01 | The initial page shall show the project title. |
| UX-02 | The initial page shall show a short description. |
| UX-03 | The initial page shall include an Enter/Explore button if appropriate. |
| UX-04 | The page shall include the 3D viewer. |
| UX-05 | Viewer controls shall be minimal and shall not cover excessive portions of the 3D environment. |
| UX-06 | Unnecessary animations or UI elements that could distract from the reconstruction shall be avoided. |

## 12. 3D Reconstruction Requirements

**Generic pipeline:**

```
Captured Video / Images
→ Frame Selection
→ Image Preprocessing
→ Feature Matching / Spatial Reconstruction
→ 3D Reconstruction
→ Model Processing
→ Web Optimization
→ Final 3D Asset
```

| ID | Requirement |
|---|---|
| RR-01 | The pipeline shall accept the captured video/images as input. |
| RR-02 | The pipeline shall produce a 3D representation of the captured environment. |
| RR-03 | The final asset shall be suitable for web visualization. |
| RR-04 | The reconstruction method shall be selected based on the captured data and competition requirements. |
| RR-05 | Reconstruction output shall be visually inspected before integration into the viewer. |

> **The reconstruction method is intentionally not specified.** Photogrammetry, Gaussian Splatting, NeRF, mesh reconstruction, and SLAM are all possible; none is assumed until the implementation team finalizes the choice. The PRD will be updated at that point.

