## 15. High-Level System Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    subgraph L1[Capture Layer]
        C1[Indoor Space] --> C2[Video / Images]
    end
    subgraph L2[Reconstruction Layer]
        R1[Preprocessing] --> R2[3D Reconstruction]
    end
    subgraph L3[Processing / Optimization Layer]
        P1[Model Processing] --> P2[Web Optimization]
    end
    subgraph L4[Web Application Layer]
        W1[Model Loader] --> W2[3D Renderer + Camera Controls]
    end
    C2 --> R1
    R2 --> P1
    P2 --> W1
    W2 --> U[User]
```

| Layer | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| **Capture Layer** | Record visual data of the physical space following the competition SOP. |
| **Reconstruction Layer** | Prepare the captured data and generate the 3D representation. |
| **Processing / Optimization Layer** | Clean and reduce the 3D asset for efficient browser delivery. |
| **Web Application Layer** | Load, render, and let the user interact with the final asset; show loading and error states. |
| **User** | Explores the environment in the browser. |

**Extensibility (Round 2 readiness):** The web application layer should keep the model loading, rendering, and camera control concerns separate from the UI, so that a future overlay layer (for example POIs) can be added without rebuilding the viewer. No such overlay is built in Round 1.

