## 18. Performance Requirements

No specific FPS or load-time figures are claimed. Targets will be set from measurements after implementation.

The system should:

- Load the 3D environment efficiently.
- Avoid unnecessarily large assets.
- Maintain responsive camera interaction.
- Use optimized textures and geometry where applicable.
- Provide loading feedback for large assets.

## 19. Error Handling

| Scenario | User-Facing Behavior | Fallback |
|---|---|---|
| 3D model fails to load | Message: the environment could not be loaded, with a retry option. | Keep the page functional; show the project description. |
| Network failure | Message: connection problem, check your network and retry. | Retry button. |
| Unsupported browser | Message: browser is not supported; suggest a modern browser. | Show project information without the 3D view. |
| Corrupted asset | Message: the model file could not be read. | Do not render partial/broken geometry; show error state. |
| Missing model | Message: the model file was not found. | Show error state; log details for developers. |
| WebGL unavailable | Message: 3D graphics are not available on this device or browser. | Show project information and the demo video link `[DEMO VIDEO URL]`. |
| Slow loading | Show a progress or loading indicator and a note that loading may take time. | Keep UI responsive; allow the user to wait or retry. |

## 20. Security Considerations

Round 1 is primarily a public visualization application.

- Do not expose API keys.
- Do not commit secrets to GitHub.
- Validate external asset paths.
- Avoid unnecessary collection of user information.
- Use HTTPS for deployment.
- Keep dependencies updated where practical.

