## 24. Constraints

- The project must follow the competition's capture SOP.
- The solution should be practical within the available development time.
- The final 3D environment must be usable in a browser.
- Large assets should be optimized.
- The project should remain maintainable for future rounds.
- The implementation should avoid unnecessary hardware dependency for the web viewer.

## 25. Assumptions

- The team has access to an indoor space for capture.
- The competition provides a capture SOP.
- The team has access to a computer capable of processing the reconstruction.
- Users will access the viewer through a modern web browser.
- The exact reconstruction technology will be finalized after evaluating the captured data.

## 26. Success Metrics

Metrics are qualitative or pass/fail unless measured later. No results are stated here.

| Metric | How It Will Be Assessed |
|---|---|
| Successful 3D reconstruction | A usable 3D representation of the space is produced. |
| Successful browser rendering | The asset renders in supported browsers. |
| Viewer usability | A first-time user can find and use the controls without help. |
| Loading reliability | The asset loads consistently across repeated tests. |
| Interactive exploration | The user can move through and inspect the space. |
| Model visual quality | Team review of the result against the captured space. |
| Web performance | Load time and interaction smoothness are measured on test devices and recorded. |
| Round 1 submission | All four deliverables are completed. |

